WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.950 --> 00:00:04.770
I'm Jenna Fisher.
我是珍娜·费舍尔。

2
00:00:04.950 --> 00:00:06.070
And I'm Angela Kinsey.
我是安吉拉·金赛。

3
00:00:06.210 --> 00:00:07.370
We were on The Office together.
我们曾一起出演《办公室》。

4
00:00:07.590 --> 00:00:08.610
And we're best friends.
我们是最好的朋友。

5
00:00:08.710 --> 00:00:12.430
And now we're doing the Ultimate Office rewatch podcast just for you.
现在我们正为你们带来终极《办公室》重温播客。

6
00:00:12.590 --> 00:00:19.410
Each week, we will break down an episode of The Office and give exclusive behind-the-scenes stories that only two people who were there can tell you.
每周，我们都会剖析一集《办公室》，并分享只有身临其境的两人才能告诉你的独家幕后故事。

7
00:00:19.590 --> 00:00:20.550
We're The Office ladies.
我们是《办公室》女士。

8
00:00:24.230 --> 00:00:25.030
Howdy, Ange.
你好啊，安吉。

9
00:00:25.490 --> 00:00:26.530
Bonjour, Jenna.
你好，珍娜。

10
00:00:28.670 --> 00:00:31.870
Oh, that's going to kind of come up later in this episode.
噢，这在这一集后面会提到。

11
00:00:32.070 --> 00:00:33.810
There's going to be some accents later.
后面会有一些口音出现。

12
00:00:33.950 --> 00:00:34.650
There are.
确实会有。

13
00:00:34.970 --> 00:00:36.470
Oh, it's fun accent day.
噢，今天是趣味口音日。

14
00:00:36.470 --> 00:00:36.970
Oh, no.
噢，不。

15
00:00:37.150 --> 00:00:38.150
People are turning us off.
大家都要关掉节目了。

16
00:00:38.370 --> 00:00:38.850
No, no, no.
不，不，不。

17
00:00:39.010 --> 00:00:39.750
They're like, oh, no.
他们会说，噢，不。

18
00:00:39.830 --> 00:00:40.650
It's accent day.
今天是口音日。

19
00:00:40.750 --> 00:00:41.370
It's okay.
没关系的。

20
00:00:41.530 --> 00:00:42.410
We won't go crazy.
我们不会太疯狂的。

21
00:00:43.230 --> 00:00:44.910
Yeah, this is a fun one, Jenna.
是啊，这一集很有趣，珍娜。

22
00:00:45.070 --> 00:00:46.030
Tell them what we're doing today.
告诉大家我们今天要讲什么。

23
00:00:46.690 --> 00:00:57.150
We are doing Product Recall Season 3, Episode 20, written by Justin Spitzer and Brent Forrester and directed by Randall Einhorn.
我们要讲的是《产品召回》，第三季第20集，由贾斯汀·斯皮策和布伦特·福雷斯特编剧，兰德尔·艾因霍恩执导。

24
00:00:57.890 --> 00:01:00.610
Randall, I was so excited when Randall got to direct.
兰德尔，当兰德尔能执导时我太兴奋了。

25
00:01:00.870 --> 00:01:01.770
We'll get into that.
我们稍后会聊到这个。

26
00:01:01.770 --> 00:01:06.530
But, you know, Randall was our cinematographer, so this was really fun for him and fun for us.
但你知道，兰德尔曾是我们的摄影指导，所以这对他是件乐事，对我们也一样。

27
00:01:06.730 --> 00:01:10.190
Did you know that Randall directed the most episodes of The Office?
你知道兰德尔执导了《办公室》最多的集数吗？

28
00:01:11.010 --> 00:01:12.550
No, I did not.
不，我不知道。

29
00:01:12.910 --> 00:01:13.650
Crazy, right?
很疯狂吧？

30
00:01:13.650 --> 00:01:15.270
I think he did 15.
我想他执导了15集。

31
00:01:15.870 --> 00:01:17.130
That is so wild.
那真是太惊人了。

32
00:01:17.250 --> 00:01:18.470
Well, I love that even more.
好吧，我更喜欢这一点了。

33
00:01:18.470 --> 00:01:23.310
Well, I am ready for a summary, Angela, but I've got a little special something.
好了，我准备好听剧情梗概了，安吉拉，但我有个特别的小玩意儿。

34
00:01:23.870 --> 00:01:24.530
Sam?
山姆？

35
00:01:25.070 --> 00:01:26.830
It's Angela and Jenna.
是安吉拉和珍娜。

36
00:01:27.090 --> 00:01:27.970
You know what?
你知道吗？

37
00:01:28.590 --> 00:01:29.670
We're the Office Episode.
我们是《办公室》剧集。

38
00:01:29.950 --> 00:01:30.970
Do-do-do-op summary.
嘟嘟嘟，剧情梗概。

39
00:01:32.050 --> 00:01:32.710
What?
什么？

40
00:01:33.390 --> 00:01:36.000
So adorable.
太可爱了。

41
00:01:36.540 --> 00:01:37.800
Isn't that so cool?
是不是很酷？

42
00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:39.120
It's so cute.
太可爱了。

43
00:01:39.120 --> 00:01:45.580
That was sent in by Joey Moisica, and he said he recorded all of the parts himself, just like Andy.
这是乔伊·莫伊西卡寄来的，他说他像安迪一样，自己录制了所有的声部。

44
00:01:45.920 --> 00:01:48.900
I was going to ask, because there's like a doo-wop part.
我正想问呢，因为里面有个嘟囔声部。

45
00:01:49.300 --> 00:01:50.260
That's so cool.
太酷了。

46
00:01:50.420 --> 00:01:51.200
Thank you, Joey.
谢谢你，乔伊。

47
00:01:52.000 --> 00:01:54.760
All right, so here is the summary for Product Recall.
好了，这就是《产品召回》的剧情梗概。

48
00:01:55.640 --> 00:02:02.740
Dunder Mifflin is in crisis mode after paper with an obscene watermark goes into circulation to customers.
邓德·米夫林公司陷入了危机模式，因为印有淫秽水印的纸张流向了客户。

49
00:02:03.560 --> 00:02:04.080
Oof.
哎哟。

50
00:02:04.440 --> 00:02:04.660
Ugh.
呃。

51
00:02:06.000 --> 00:02:10.600
Michael organizes a press conference and apologizes to a client.
迈克尔组织了一场新闻发布会，并向一位客户道歉。

52
00:02:11.120 --> 00:02:17.820
When the client demands that Michael be fired, Michael recruits Pam and Dwight to help him make an apology video.
当客户要求开除迈克尔时，迈克尔找来帕姆和德怀特帮他制作了一段道歉视频。

53
00:02:18.300 --> 00:02:22.260
The accountants learn how to make customer service calls from Kelly,
会计们向凯莉学习如何接听客户服务电话，

54
00:02:22.540 --> 00:02:28.220
and Creed, who is determined to save his job, pins the blame on an employee at the paper mill.
而一心想保住工作的克里德则把责任推卸给造纸厂的一名员工。

55
00:02:28.700 --> 00:02:30.160
Poor Debbie Brown.
可怜的黛比·布朗。

56
00:02:30.460 --> 00:02:31.600
Oh, poor Debbie.
噢，可怜的黛比。

57
00:02:32.340 --> 00:02:34.400
This was such a fun episode.
这一集真是有趣。

58
00:02:34.660 --> 00:02:36.200
I loved re-watching it.
我重温的时候很喜欢。

59
00:02:36.280 --> 00:02:37.520
I had so many fun memories.
我有很多美好的回忆。

60
00:02:38.380 --> 00:02:38.840
Same.
我也是。

61
00:02:39.600 --> 00:02:40.440
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

62
00:02:40.520 --> 00:02:43.760
I feel like Steve is in rare form in this episode.
我觉得史蒂夫在这一集里的状态真是难得一见。

63
00:02:43.980 --> 00:02:50.160
I also personally think some of the best quotes of the whole season three are in this episode.
我个人也认为第三季中一些最棒的台词都出自这一集。

64
00:02:50.360 --> 00:02:51.040
Oh, yes.
噢，没错。

65
00:02:51.220 --> 00:02:52.400
It's so many.
实在太多了。

66
00:02:52.540 --> 00:02:53.120
We'll get to it.
我们待会儿会讲到。

67
00:02:53.220 --> 00:02:58.780
And I just want to share one of my favorite quotes of the whole entire series is in this episode.
而且我只想分享一下，我最喜欢的整部剧的台词之一就在这一集里。

68
00:02:59.340 --> 00:02:59.620
Oh.
噢。

69
00:03:00.020 --> 00:03:00.340
Rare.
难得。

70
00:03:02.200 --> 00:03:04.460
This is also the episode of Animal Noises.
这一集也是“动物叫声”那一集。

71
00:03:04.460 --> 00:03:06.820
Or nonverbal reactions.
或者说非语言反应。

72
00:03:07.180 --> 00:03:07.380
Yeah.
是啊。

73
00:03:07.640 --> 00:03:09.400
Accents and nonverbals.
口音和非语言表达。

74
00:03:09.840 --> 00:03:11.320
Someone just hit fast forward.
有人刚才按了快进。

75
00:03:11.680 --> 00:03:12.500
Oh, no.
噢，不。

76
00:03:13.000 --> 00:03:14.780
Well, fast fact number one.
好吧，第一个冷知识。

77
00:03:14.920 --> 00:03:19.240
I mentioned that this episode was written by both Justin Spitzer and Brent Forrester.
我提到过这一集是由贾斯汀·斯皮策和布伦特·福雷斯特共同编写的。

78
00:03:19.480 --> 00:03:24.280
I should probably clarify that there are some writers who work in teaMs.
我可能应该澄清一下，有些编剧是团队合作的。

79
00:03:24.740 --> 00:03:25.080
Yes.
是的。

80
00:03:25.100 --> 00:03:27.460
Like we've mentioned before, Gene and Lee.
就像我们之前提到的，吉恩和李。

81
00:03:27.460 --> 00:03:28.900
They were a writing team.
他们是一个编剧搭档。

82
00:03:29.040 --> 00:03:30.920
They were hired together as a duo.
他们是作为二人组一起被雇佣的。

83
00:03:31.160 --> 00:03:34.120
But Justin and Brent were not a writing team.
但贾斯汀和布伦特并不是编剧搭档。

84
00:03:34.300 --> 00:03:35.880
They were hired separately.
他们是分别被雇佣的。

85
00:03:35.960 --> 00:03:39.820
So this was interesting that they were co-writing this together.
所以他们能共同编写这一集很有意思。

86
00:03:39.820 --> 00:03:45.340
Well, we reached out to both of them to hear what it was like to be paired together on this episode.
我们联系了他们俩，想听听他们被凑在一起编写这一集是什么感觉。

87
00:03:45.520 --> 00:03:49.900
So they said that Greg just paired them together because he thought it would be kind of fun.
他们说格雷格把他们凑在一起，只是因为他觉得这样会很有趣。

88
00:03:50.500 --> 00:03:55.640
And Justin told me that they basically just split it down the middle, that Brent took a pass at act one.
贾斯汀告诉我，他们基本上就是平分了工作，布伦特负责第一幕。

89
00:03:55.940 --> 00:03:57.260
Justin did act two.
贾斯汀负责第二幕。

90
00:03:57.440 --> 00:03:58.820
And then they split act three.
然后他们平分了第三幕。

91
00:03:59.220 --> 00:04:02.660
And then they came together one afternoon and they kind of went over it.
之后他们在一个下午聚在一起，把剧本过了一遍。

92
00:04:03.140 --> 00:04:08.980
And since Brent was the senior writer, he kind of took the lead on a kind of a dual rewrite.
由于布伦特是资深编剧，他在某种程度上的双人重写工作中起到了主导作用。

93
00:04:09.540 --> 00:04:14.900
And then they turned it in and it was kind of, you know, punched up by the staff like every other episode.
然后他们交了稿，就像其他剧集一样，由全体编剧进行了润色。

94
00:04:15.360 --> 00:04:20.660
I could see Greg doing this because he loved pairing together people to see what would come out of that pairing.
我能理解格雷格为什么这么做，因为他喜欢把人凑在一起，看看这种组合会产生什么火花。

95
00:04:20.820 --> 00:04:24.820
Whether it was characters or writers, you know, he loved to see what happened.
无论是角色还是编剧，你知道的，他喜欢看会发生什么。

96
00:04:25.060 --> 00:04:27.680
Even our editors sometimes were paired up in different ways.
甚至我们的剪辑师有时也会以不同的方式进行搭档。

97
00:04:28.580 --> 00:04:37.640
Well, Brent said that it's true that Greg did make it clear that he was the senior writer and that he had final decision on what went into the draft.
布伦特说，格雷格确实明确表示他是资深编剧，并且对草稿的最终内容拥有决定权，这是事实。

98
00:04:37.640 --> 00:04:47.840
But he said right from the start, he could see that Justin's scenes were just so good that it would be a terrible mistake to put, quote, my grubby fingers on any of it, end quote.
但他从一开始就说，他看出贾斯汀写的场景太棒了，如果把“我那双脏手”——引用他的原话——伸过去改动任何地方，那将是一个可怕的错误。

99
00:04:49.320 --> 00:04:53.740
So he said that they didn't change any of each other's work.
所以他说他们没有改动对方的任何作品。

100
00:04:53.900 --> 00:04:57.280
They ended up turning it in just as they had both originally written it.
他们最终交上去的稿子，就是他们各自最初写出来的样子。

101
00:04:57.500 --> 00:04:58.920
Well, that is so fun.
哇，那太有趣了。

102
00:04:59.340 --> 00:04:59.520
All right.
好吧。

103
00:04:59.640 --> 00:05:00.660
Fast fact number two.
第二个速览事实。

104
00:05:01.220 --> 00:05:06.040
I asked these guys, what was the inspiration for this episode?
我问了这些人，这一集的灵感来源是什么？

105
00:05:06.040 --> 00:05:08.780
Was this based on anything in real life?
它是基于现实生活中的什么事情吗？

106
00:05:08.980 --> 00:05:17.960
And Justin told me that he couldn't remember exactly where the idea came from, but he's pretty sure that it just came out of one of those pitch sessions in the room.
贾斯汀告诉我，他不记得这个点子具体是怎么来的了，但他很确定它就是在那间屋子里的头脑风暴会议中产生的。

107
00:05:17.980 --> 00:05:24.640
So it wasn't like one writer had the idea, but it was sort of a collective, one of your group mind things, Ange.
所以并不是某个编剧想到的，而是一种集体创作，安吉，就像你们那种集体思维一样。

108
00:05:24.820 --> 00:05:26.540
Oh, I like group mind.
哦，我喜欢“集体思维”这个说法。

109
00:05:26.820 --> 00:05:29.620
Well, he said he does have a very distinct memory.
嗯，他说他确实有一个非常清晰的记忆。

110
00:05:29.620 --> 00:05:37.300
As they were circling closer and closer to something that felt like an episode, Lee Eisenberg suddenly blurted out, a product recall.
当他们越来越接近一个感觉像是这一集主题的内容时，李·艾森伯格突然脱口而出：产品召回。

111
00:05:37.420 --> 00:05:38.780
It's a product recall.
就是产品召回。

112
00:05:39.120 --> 00:05:45.720
And after Lee said that, they knew it was going to be like a defective product and a mini scandal.
李说完之后，他们就知道这会是关于一个有缺陷的产品和一场小型丑闻的故事。

113
00:05:46.180 --> 00:05:47.800
But here's the thing, Ange.
但重点是，安吉。

114
00:05:47.880 --> 00:05:49.280
Here is why I asked.
这就是我为什么要问的原因。

115
00:05:49.480 --> 00:05:51.580
I did a little Googling.
我稍微查了一下谷歌。

116
00:05:51.580 --> 00:06:03.280
This episode aired in April 2007, and the crazy thing is that in August of 2007, there was a massive, historic Mattel toy recall.
这一集是在2007年4月播出的，疯狂的是，在2007年8月，美泰公司发生了一次大规模、史无前例的玩具召回事件。

117
00:06:04.340 --> 00:06:06.100
A huge product recall.
一次巨大的产品召回。

118
00:06:06.260 --> 00:06:07.440
What did they recall?
他们召回了什么？

119
00:06:07.680 --> 00:06:10.260
They recalled 19 million toys.
他们召回了1900万件玩具。

120
00:06:10.620 --> 00:06:11.700
What was it?
那是什么？

121
00:06:12.200 --> 00:06:15.220
Some of them were recalled because they had lead paint.
其中一些被召回是因为含有铅漆。

122
00:06:15.660 --> 00:06:16.760
Was it a G.I.
是特种部队吗？

123
00:06:16.860 --> 00:06:17.020
Joe?
乔？

124
00:06:17.260 --> 00:06:18.480
No, I don't know what it was.
不，我不知道具体是什么。

125
00:06:18.480 --> 00:06:21.160
A bunch of toys that were shown to have lead paint.
是一堆被发现含有铅漆的玩具。

126
00:06:21.160 --> 00:06:26.560
And the other was because there was a tiny magnet that kept falling off, and it posed a choking hazard.
还有一些是因为有一个小磁铁总是掉下来，造成了窒息危险。

127
00:06:27.500 --> 00:06:32.240
But also in 2007, there was a massive crib recall.
而且在2007年，还有一次大规模的婴儿床召回事件。

128
00:06:32.980 --> 00:06:36.360
One million Graco and Simplicity cribs were recalled.
一百万张Graco和Simplicity品牌的婴儿床被召回。

129
00:06:36.600 --> 00:06:43.700
And I even read an article that called 2007, quote, the year of the recall.
我甚至读到一篇文章，称2007年为“召回之年”。

130
00:06:44.240 --> 00:06:45.660
Well, that's crazy.
哇，那太疯狂了。

131
00:06:45.660 --> 00:06:47.520
I wonder if it was in the zeitgeiSt.
我在想这是否是当时的一种时代精神。

132
00:06:47.680 --> 00:06:50.120
It was in the group mind of the world.
那是全世界的集体思维。

133
00:06:50.120 --> 00:06:54.820
And it went into Lee's brain, and he shouted it into the writer's room.
它进入了李的大脑，然后他把它喊进了编剧室。

134
00:06:55.000 --> 00:06:57.160
And it became an episode of The Office.
于是它就成了《办公室》的一集。

135
00:06:57.540 --> 00:06:58.600
Major group mind.
重大的集体思维。

136
00:06:58.800 --> 00:07:00.100
That's some global group mind.
那可是全球性的集体思维。

137
00:07:00.420 --> 00:07:03.180
Okay, lady, I'm going to move us along to fast fact number three.
好了，女士，我要带我们进入第三个速览事实了。

138
00:07:03.420 --> 00:07:05.520
I'm calling it location alert.
我把它叫做“取景地提醒”。

139
00:07:06.320 --> 00:07:06.840
Okay.
好的。

140
00:07:07.600 --> 00:07:13.540
As part of this episode, Jim and Andy go to a local high school to apologize for the obscene watermark.
在这一集中，吉姆和安迪去了一所当地的高中，为那个淫秽的水印道歉。

141
00:07:14.260 --> 00:07:17.420
And Kentopedia let us know, because we got some mail.
肯托百科（Kentopedia）告诉了我们，因为我们收到了一些邮件。

142
00:07:17.600 --> 00:07:20.680
People wanted to know, was this the same school where we shot Diwali?
人们想知道，这和我们拍摄《排灯节》那一集是同一所学校吗？

143
00:07:21.060 --> 00:07:23.080
People love to know about locations.
人们很喜欢了解取景地。

144
00:07:23.400 --> 00:07:24.400
They love it.
他们非常喜欢。

145
00:07:25.500 --> 00:07:28.700
This was filmed at a different school than Diwali.
这次拍摄的学校和《排灯节》那次不一样。

146
00:07:29.000 --> 00:07:32.660
This time we filmed at St. John Paul Academy in Burbank.
这次我们是在伯班克的圣约翰保罗学院拍摄的。

147
00:07:33.020 --> 00:07:37.520
In real life, it is a private Catholic STEM immersion high school.
在现实生活中，这是一所私立的天主教STEM沉浸式高中。

148
00:07:37.760 --> 00:07:40.780
The school colors are white, blue, and red.
学校的校色是白色、蓝色和红色。

149
00:07:41.000 --> 00:07:43.120
And the real students at the school wear uniforMs.
学校里的真实学生都穿着制服。

150
00:07:43.980 --> 00:07:47.420
For our shoot, we hired background performers to play the students.
为了拍摄，我们雇佣了临时演员来扮演学生。

151
00:07:47.600 --> 00:07:50.860
We did not use the actual students of this school.
我们没有使用这所学校的真实学生。

152
00:07:51.100 --> 00:07:56.060
I feel like that is a thorough answer to this location question.
我觉得对于这个地点的问题，这已经是一个详尽的回答了。

153
00:07:56.440 --> 00:07:56.860
Yeah.
没错。

154
00:07:57.260 --> 00:07:59.260
You know, I went to a Catholic high school.
你知道吗，我上的是一所天主教高中。

155
00:07:59.680 --> 00:08:00.420
I know this.
我知道。

156
00:08:00.440 --> 00:08:01.280
It was not co-ed.
那不是男女同校的。

157
00:08:01.520 --> 00:08:03.060
It was all girls.
那是所女校。

158
00:08:03.340 --> 00:08:04.600
And I wore a uniform.
而且我得穿校服。

159
00:08:04.600 --> 00:08:09.140
And our colors were green and white and gray and navy.
我们的校色是绿色、白色、灰色和海军蓝。

160
00:08:09.300 --> 00:08:11.480
I think were the colors we were allowed to wear.
我想我们被允许穿的颜色就是这些。

161
00:08:11.600 --> 00:08:11.960
And yellow.
还有黄色。

162
00:08:11.960 --> 00:08:12.020
Yellow.
黄色。

163
00:08:12.340 --> 00:08:13.540
That's a lot of colors.
那颜色也太多了。

164
00:08:14.640 --> 00:08:16.120
It's really only five.
其实只有五种而已。

165
00:08:16.580 --> 00:08:19.200
And you're only allowed to wear those colors.
而且你只能穿这些颜色的衣服。

166
00:08:19.420 --> 00:08:20.200
Seems like a lot.
感觉还是很多。

167
00:08:20.700 --> 00:08:21.400
Scale it back.
精简一下吧。

168
00:08:21.620 --> 00:08:23.460
Do you wear...
你穿……

169
00:08:25.260 --> 00:08:26.580
How many colors do you wear?
你平时穿几种颜色？

170
00:08:26.840 --> 00:08:30.160
I just grab whatever's, you know, there.
我就是随手抓起手边有的衣服穿。

171
00:08:31.100 --> 00:08:31.620
Right.
也是。

172
00:08:31.820 --> 00:08:36.240
So imagine you're getting dressed in the morning and you have to limit it to only these five colors.
所以想象一下，你早上穿衣服时必须限制只能穿这五种颜色。

173
00:08:36.460 --> 00:08:37.020
Well, listen.
好吧，听着。

174
00:08:37.200 --> 00:08:39.400
A friend of mine did that thing.
我有个朋友做过那种测试。

175
00:08:39.540 --> 00:08:41.860
Remember when ladies would get their colors done?
还记得以前女士们会去做色彩鉴定吗？

176
00:08:42.400 --> 00:08:43.080
Oh, yes.
哦，记得。

177
00:08:43.240 --> 00:08:45.000
And you find out if you're like fall or spring.
就是去测测你是秋季型还是春季型。

178
00:08:45.000 --> 00:08:46.960
A summer or a winter or something.
或者是夏季型、冬季型之类的。

179
00:08:47.080 --> 00:08:47.900
My mom did this.
我妈做过这个。

180
00:08:48.000 --> 00:08:49.020
My mom was a summer.
我妈是夏季型的。

181
00:08:49.440 --> 00:08:49.880
Okay.
好吧。

182
00:08:50.200 --> 00:08:52.800
So a friend of mine recently did this.
我有个朋友最近也做了这个。

183
00:08:52.980 --> 00:08:54.620
Wait, they're still doing this?
等等，现在还有人在做这个？

184
00:08:54.680 --> 00:08:55.600
They're still doing it.
还在做呢。

185
00:08:55.720 --> 00:08:57.580
It sort of went out of fashion, but whatever.
虽然这已经有点过时了，但无所谓。

186
00:08:57.760 --> 00:08:58.860
She did it.
她做了。

187
00:08:58.860 --> 00:09:04.000
And she found out that she's like shades of blue and coral and white.
结果发现她适合蓝色、珊瑚色和白色系的颜色。

188
00:09:04.000 --> 00:09:07.240
And she just filled her closet with those colors.
于是她就把衣柜全换成了这些颜色。

189
00:09:07.480 --> 00:09:08.760
She's always in those three colors.
她总是穿着这三种颜色的衣服。

190
00:09:09.700 --> 00:09:10.580
So what it...
那她……

191
00:09:10.580 --> 00:09:11.260
Do you know what she is?
你知道她属于哪种类型吗？

192
00:09:11.340 --> 00:09:12.180
Is that summer?
那是夏季型吗？

193
00:09:12.460 --> 00:09:13.180
I don't know.
我不知道。

194
00:09:13.380 --> 00:09:14.060
Coral, blue, and white?
珊瑚色、蓝色和白色？

195
00:09:14.380 --> 00:09:15.280
I don't know what it is.
我不知道那是什么类型。

196
00:09:15.640 --> 00:09:16.460
Maybe spring.
可能是春季型吧。

197
00:09:16.760 --> 00:09:19.760
But listen, it's a commitment to stay in those three colors.
但听着，只穿那三种颜色真的需要很大的决心。

198
00:09:20.060 --> 00:09:21.100
I'd have a hard time.
我可做不到。

199
00:09:21.820 --> 00:09:22.560
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

200
00:09:22.560 --> 00:09:24.520
This is literally what I was saying.
这不就是我刚才说的嘛。

201
00:09:24.520 --> 00:09:27.000
I said I could only wear five colors.
我说过我只能穿五种颜色。

202
00:09:27.000 --> 00:09:28.640
And you're like, it's a lot of colors.
而你却说，这已经很多种颜色了。

203
00:09:28.640 --> 00:09:30.000
I don't see what the issue is.
我不觉得这有什么问题。

204
00:09:30.100 --> 00:09:33.020
And now you're like, I would have a hard time only wearing a few colors.
现在你又说，只穿几种颜色对你来说很难。

205
00:09:33.260 --> 00:09:39.180
My point was, if you're going to have a school that has uniforms, you can't have a lot of options.
我的意思是，如果学校要统一校服，就不能提供太多选择。

206
00:09:40.420 --> 00:09:40.880
Why?
为什么？

207
00:09:41.560 --> 00:09:42.520
Because you're already...
因为你已经……

208
00:09:42.520 --> 00:09:45.340
You can't have personal expression within uniform?
校服里就不能有个人表达吗？

209
00:09:45.780 --> 00:09:46.120
No.
不能。

210
00:09:46.600 --> 00:09:47.540
Oh, my gosh.
天哪。

211
00:09:47.560 --> 00:09:48.500
You're taking a stand.
你这是在表明立场啊。

212
00:09:48.740 --> 00:09:54.440
You've clearly not thought about this at all because you are taking multiple positions on this.
你显然根本没考虑过这个问题，因为你在这件事上立场反复。

213
00:09:54.520 --> 00:09:55.200
That's one subject.
那是一个主题。

214
00:09:55.380 --> 00:10:00.420
What's the point of having a uniform if you can have multiple colors and freedom of expression?
如果可以有多种颜色和表达自由，那穿校服还有什么意义？

215
00:10:00.640 --> 00:10:01.700
There's no point.
毫无意义。

216
00:10:02.240 --> 00:10:04.060
Either have a uniform or don't.
要么穿校服，要么别穿。

217
00:10:04.440 --> 00:10:04.760
All right.
好吧。

218
00:10:04.840 --> 00:10:07.180
Well, we had to all wear the same skirt.
我们当时都得穿一样的裙子。

219
00:10:07.180 --> 00:10:08.080
It was the same.
都是一样的。

220
00:10:08.220 --> 00:10:09.160
There was no choice.
没得选。

221
00:10:09.520 --> 00:10:11.160
Or navy pants.
或者藏青色的裤子。

222
00:10:11.360 --> 00:10:14.380
Or a yellow shirt or a green shirt or a white shirt.
或者黄衬衫、绿衬衫、白衬衫。

223
00:10:14.880 --> 00:10:17.200
We have to be done talking about this.
我们必须结束这个话题了。

224
00:10:17.440 --> 00:10:19.780
On top, you could wear the different colors.
上衣可以穿不同颜色的。

225
00:10:20.060 --> 00:10:24.220
But they had to be a collared shirt and you couldn't have any logo.
但必须是有领的衬衫，而且不能有任何标志。

226
00:10:24.520 --> 00:10:24.860
Logos.
标志。

227
00:10:25.080 --> 00:10:25.820
No logos.
不准有标志。

228
00:10:26.180 --> 00:10:34.000
Not even like, you know, some people, they would try to sneak in like a little polo on their lapel.
甚至连那种，你知道，有些人会试图在翻领上偷偷弄个小马标。

229
00:10:34.120 --> 00:10:35.060
And that would be a no.
那也是不行的。

230
00:10:35.760 --> 00:10:36.040
Wow.
哇。

231
00:10:37.100 --> 00:10:37.920
Because that...
因为那……

232
00:10:38.080 --> 00:10:39.360
Lock it up, uniform.
管好它，校服。

233
00:10:39.660 --> 00:10:40.240
Lock it up.
管好它。

234
00:10:40.860 --> 00:10:42.060
Lady, where are we?
女士，我们这是在哪儿？

235
00:10:42.300 --> 00:10:43.820
Well, we're ready to take a break.
我们要休息一下了。

236
00:10:43.820 --> 00:10:46.060
And then we're going to come back and break down this episode.
回来之后我们要深入解析这一集。

237
00:10:46.300 --> 00:10:50.740
Well, before we take a break, I want to just share one thing about this episode.
好吧，在休息之前，我想分享关于这一集的一件事。

238
00:10:51.940 --> 00:10:54.520
Ah, well, I'll just get to it.
啊，好吧，我就直说了。

239
00:10:55.200 --> 00:10:56.160
What is it?
是什么？

240
00:10:57.100 --> 00:11:00.980
I had the hugest zit on my cheek.
我脸颊上长了个巨大的痘痘。

241
00:11:01.280 --> 00:11:05.020
And I remember being really bummed out because I had a nice big storyline.
我记得当时特别沮丧，因为我那一集戏份很重。

242
00:11:05.040 --> 00:11:08.000
And I woke up with an enormous zit on my cheek.
结果我醒来发现脸颊上长了个巨大的痘痘。

243
00:11:08.240 --> 00:11:09.920
And they tried to cover it with makeup.
他们试图用化妆品遮住它。

244
00:11:10.040 --> 00:11:13.000
Jenna, they didn't splurge for CGI and scoochy it out.
珍娜，他们可没花钱用CGI把它修掉。

245
00:11:13.360 --> 00:11:14.780
It's in the whole episode.
整集里都有它。

246
00:11:15.220 --> 00:11:16.660
There's so much makeup on it.
上面涂了厚厚的遮瑕。

247
00:11:16.660 --> 00:11:18.760
It's like an orange patch on my cheek.
就像我脸颊上贴了一块橙色的补丁。

248
00:11:19.580 --> 00:11:21.480
I did not notice it one time.
我一次都没注意到。

249
00:11:21.620 --> 00:11:22.680
It's on my left cheek.
就在我的左脸颊上。

250
00:11:22.700 --> 00:11:23.080
In watching this.
看这一集的时候。

251
00:11:23.740 --> 00:11:25.620
Do you have time codes for it?
你有这段的时间码吗？

252
00:11:25.700 --> 00:11:27.780
Is that something we can look forward to after the break?
那是我们休息后可以期待的内容吗？

253
00:11:27.840 --> 00:11:28.240
Yes.
是的。

254
00:11:28.760 --> 00:11:29.160
Yes.
是的。

255
00:11:29.420 --> 00:11:30.380
Well, there you go, guys.
好了，就是这样，伙计们。

256
00:11:30.380 --> 00:11:31.080
If you want a close up.
如果你想要特写的话。

257
00:11:31.220 --> 00:11:33.080
Well, listen, I'm sure you're riveted now.
听着，我相信你们现在一定被深深吸引了。

258
00:11:33.300 --> 00:11:34.520
You can't wait to come back.
迫不及待想回来了吧。

259
00:11:34.760 --> 00:11:35.960
We're going to take a break.
我们要休息一下。

260
00:11:36.160 --> 00:11:37.500
Come back with this episode.
回来继续这一集。

261
00:11:46.830 --> 00:11:50.890
Okay, so we start off this episode with a very funny cold open.
好的，这一集我们以一个非常有趣的开场戏开始。

262
00:11:50.890 --> 00:11:55.670
I think it is one of the classics of all the cold opens on the whole series.
我认为这是整部剧所有开场戏中的经典之一。

263
00:11:56.150 --> 00:11:56.670
100%.
百分之百。

264
00:11:56.670 --> 00:12:05.610
It is Jim dressed as Dwight, acting like Dwight, and it makes Dwight crazy in some of the best
那是吉姆打扮成德怀特，模仿德怀特的样子，这让德怀特抓狂，而且在这个开场戏里有

265
00:12:05.610 --> 00:12:07.110
lines right here in this cold open.
一些最棒的台词。

266
00:12:07.550 --> 00:12:11.950
Lady, I remember filming this episode, and John Krasinski was so funny.
蕾迪，我记得拍摄这一集的时候，约翰·卡拉辛斯基太搞笑了。

267
00:12:12.230 --> 00:12:14.070
We could not hold it together.
我们根本憋不住笑。

268
00:12:14.310 --> 00:12:16.390
Well, we all knew how great he was at impressions.
嗯，我们都知道他模仿得有多好。

269
00:12:16.390 --> 00:12:21.310
And so when he got to actually flex that a little, we were just like, ah, I can't wait
所以当他真的能稍微展示一下时，我们当时就想，啊，我迫不及待

270
00:12:21.310 --> 00:12:21.770
to watch.
想看了。

271
00:12:22.030 --> 00:12:27.930
Well, Angela, I think this cold open has two of our most quoted moments.
嗯，安吉拉，我认为这个开场戏有两个我们被引用最多的时刻。

272
00:12:28.170 --> 00:12:29.070
For sure.
肯定的。

273
00:12:29.630 --> 00:12:33.490
Number one, Bears beats Battlestar Galactica.
第一，熊、甜菜、太空堡垒卡拉狄加。

274
00:12:33.730 --> 00:12:35.630
I mean, how many t-shirts is that on?
我是说，这印在多少件T恤上啊？

275
00:12:35.750 --> 00:12:36.350
It's on everything.
什么东西上都有。

276
00:12:36.690 --> 00:12:40.270
And also, identity theft is not a joke, Jim.
还有，身份盗用可不是开玩笑的，吉姆。

277
00:12:40.750 --> 00:12:42.930
Millions of families suffer every year.
每年有数百万个家庭深受其害。

278
00:12:43.230 --> 00:12:44.010
That's right.
没错。

279
00:12:44.210 --> 00:12:45.930
I see that all the time.
我经常看到这个。

280
00:12:46.910 --> 00:12:48.130
Identity theft is not a joke.
身份盗用可不是开玩笑的。

281
00:12:48.310 --> 00:12:51.810
Don't we sell pencils that say, identity theft is not a joke?
我们不是卖印有“身份盗用可不是开玩笑的”字样的铅笔吗？

282
00:12:51.930 --> 00:12:54.450
Don't we have a pencil pack on officeladies.com?
我们在officeladies.com上不是有铅笔套装吗？

283
00:12:54.750 --> 00:12:55.190
Yes.
是的。

284
00:12:55.590 --> 00:12:57.190
And we have that quote, right?
我们有那句台词，对吧？

285
00:12:57.410 --> 00:12:57.950
We have that quote.
我们有那句台词。

286
00:12:57.950 --> 00:13:00.190
And we also have Bears beats Battlestar Galactica.
而且我们还有“熊、甜菜、太空堡垒卡拉狄加”。

287
00:13:00.770 --> 00:13:02.490
It's just one of my favorite quotes.
这简直是我最喜欢的台词之一。

288
00:13:02.610 --> 00:13:04.990
It is not my favorite quote of the whole episode, though.
不过，这并不是我整集中最喜欢的台词。

289
00:13:05.150 --> 00:13:05.890
We'll get to that.
我们稍后会讲到。

290
00:13:06.030 --> 00:13:08.510
But this couplet is so fun.
但这组对白太有趣了。

291
00:13:08.510 --> 00:13:12.710
And I have seen people, like, at conventions and stuff say this.
我见过人们，比如在漫展之类的场合说这段话。

292
00:13:12.830 --> 00:13:13.130
False.
错误。

293
00:13:13.350 --> 00:13:13.790
Black bear.
黑熊。

294
00:13:13.910 --> 00:13:14.930
Like, the whole thing.
就像，整段话都背下来了。

295
00:13:15.310 --> 00:13:15.990
Oh, yeah.
哦，没错。

296
00:13:16.070 --> 00:13:17.110
Let's, we should play it.
我们，我们应该播放它。

297
00:13:17.210 --> 00:13:17.470
Sam.
萨姆。

298
00:13:17.550 --> 00:13:18.410
Yeah, let's play it.
是的，播放吧。

299
00:13:18.570 --> 00:13:19.250
Play this clip.
播放这段剪辑。

300
00:13:20.110 --> 00:13:20.630
Question.
提问。

301
00:13:21.090 --> 00:13:23.070
What kind of bear is best?
哪种熊最厉害？

302
00:13:24.090 --> 00:13:25.570
That's a ridiculous question.
这问题太荒谬了。

303
00:13:25.770 --> 00:13:26.070
False.
错。

304
00:13:26.370 --> 00:13:27.050
Black bear.
黑熊。

305
00:13:27.550 --> 00:13:28.350
That's debatable.
这还有待商榷。

306
00:13:28.650 --> 00:13:30.610
There are basically two schools of thought.
基本上有两种流派。

307
00:13:30.690 --> 00:13:31.010
Fact.
事实。

308
00:13:31.370 --> 00:13:32.690
Bears eat beets.
熊吃甜菜。

309
00:13:32.690 --> 00:13:36.770
Bears beets Battlestar Galactica.
熊、甜菜、《太空堡垒卡拉狄加》。

310
00:13:37.070 --> 00:13:37.490
Bears do not.
熊才不吃。

311
00:13:38.170 --> 00:13:39.570
What is going on?
到底怎么回事？

312
00:13:39.750 --> 00:13:40.870
What are you doing?
你在干什么？

313
00:13:41.950 --> 00:13:43.630
I love it so much.
我太喜欢这个了。

314
00:13:43.810 --> 00:13:46.970
I want to know, what are the two schools of thoughts about bears?
我想知道，关于熊的那两个流派是什么？

315
00:13:47.270 --> 00:13:48.750
We never find out.
我们永远没能知道。

316
00:13:48.890 --> 00:13:49.490
We don't.
确实没能知道。

317
00:13:49.610 --> 00:13:57.150
Listen, we had a fan question from Ashley Trick, Emily Dennis, Faith L, Rianne Holib, and Tara Laporte.
听着，我们收到了来自Ashley Trick、Emily Dennis、Faith L、Rianne Holib和Tara Laporte的粉丝提问。

318
00:13:57.710 --> 00:14:00.650
Basically, they all said the same version of this.
基本上，她们问的都是同一个问题。

319
00:14:00.650 --> 00:14:04.450
Please, please, please tell us everything about the cold open.
求求你们，一定要告诉我们关于那个开场戏的一切。

320
00:14:04.770 --> 00:14:07.590
